+# Phase guidance and execution repair
+
+Owner direction: Harness supplies research logic, memory and phase acceptance;
+the sustained worker adapts methods/code/settings from actual GPU debugging.
+No per-edit/per-prepare formal experiment review or small-agent dispatch.
+
+Root cause: valid C/D development passed canonical execution validation but
+_coverage_tasks then required legacy E experiment bindings. Staged preparation
+also required future experiment code to appear in the current job. Nonterminal
+worker failures were decoded as scientific completion and repeatedly rejected.
+
+Implementation:
+- Reuse existing coverage obligation.task_ids for C/D development calls; preserve
+  exact executable provenance, target, predecessors and pending scoring.
+- Treat experiment-wide math/code mappings as context for staged work. Stage
+  descriptor pins actual code; export still checks its implementation.
+- Accept a separate nonterminal checkpoint before scientific-result parsing.
+  Preserve phase/science/accounting; wait until dependency/runtime change or
+  explicit resume. Pin checkpoint bytes in the recovery handoff.
+- Repeated unchanged interface rejection parks rather than starting new workers.
+  Signature includes current phase and worker-local evidence progress.
+- Keep B05/M05 evidence acceptance and formal E binding/freeze checks.
+
+Validation: regression first on authorized hn01, full phase-native request through
+real proposal/admission/registration/execution/receipt, durable checkpoint/wake,
+formal E rejection, unlinked work rejection, full GPU-host runtime/plugin suites.
+Then build .10 on hn01, install main/private plugins/runtime, adopt at a quiet
+paused boundary retaining all accepted evidence/usage, and resume the existing C.
