+# Harness .10: phase guidance and actual GPU-driven work
+
+The owner explicitly requested sufficient autonomy: Harness guides research logic,
+shared memory and phase acceptance; actual GPU observations drive implementation.
+Initial mathematical ideas, code and settings can be revised inside one worker.
+
+Changed: C/D development reuses coverage task links, removing the accidental
+formal E experiment-binding requirement. Staged preparation executes its declared
+code; broader mathematical/control mappings remain context. Formal E comparison
+and scientific phase acceptance still require their actual evidence.
+
+Added: nonterminal phase checkpoints retain current phase, evidence and usage.
+Unchanged dependencies cause waiting, not another worker. Dependency/runtime
+changes or explicit resume recover the checkpoint. Repeated unchanged interface
+rejections also park. Failed trials and unknown execution identities are retained.
+
+Production-request preflight: the actual previously rejected
+spectrum.C.prepare.e1.a14 request passed repaired _proposal on a copied controller
+on hn01, with16 pending obligations preserved. This was admission-only replay,
+not native dispatch, a benchmark result or scientific acceptance.
+
+Independent static review identified progress-fingerprint and checkpoint-pin
+issues; both were fixed and re-reviewed without remaining blocking findings.
+All executable tests/builds run on the authorized hn01 host. Mac orchestration
+and deployment inspection do not run research workloads.
+
+GPU-host final runtime suite:468 passed in229.782s. Plugin suite:34 passed.
+Skill suite:930 run,8 text-policy assertions failed,9 skipped; baseline comparison
+is recorded separately. No full-Skill-suite success is claimed. Initial runtime
+fixture failure was corrected (distinct objective and authorization inputs), and
+all468 runtime tests were rerun successfully. Actual production-request admission
+and full real native-request execution are separate from scientific evidence.
+
+Baseline .9 Skill suite:930 run in74.294s, the identical8 failing test names and
+9 skipped. These inherited Chat/project-cooperation prose assertions are unchanged
+by this repair; they remain visible in skill.log and skill-baseline-nine.log.
